  "body": "### What is the issue with the URL Pattern Standard?\n\nNamely, for step 12.2 of https://urlpattern.spec.whatwg.org/#url-pattern-match\n\nFrom what I understand, `input` is guaranteed to be a USVString by this point:\n\n> 2. If input is a [USVString](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#idl-USVString):\n\nThis means that step 1 of:\n\n> 1. Let url be input.\n\nAnd step 3 of:\n\n> 3. [Assert](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#assert): url is a [URL](https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-url).\n\nAre confusing since if `input` were not a USVString, then the assertion on step 3 would fail since we are otherwise not going through the URL parser.\n\nI believe we can:\n- Remove step 1.\n- Change step 2 to an assert, and remove the nesting of the code in the if statement block\n- Change step 2.3 to be \"Let url\" instead of a setter\n- Remove the assertion of url being a URL record.",
